iu.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Du Wenxiu</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Du Wenxiu was the leader of the Panthay Rebellion of Hui Muslims in Yunnan against the Qing dynasty.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/du-yu-king-of-shu"><span class="enc-name">Du Yu (king of Shu)</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Du Yu, also known as Emperor Wang (Wangdi), is a legendary king of Shu who, according to later Chinese texts, taught his people agriculture.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/du-yuesheng"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/du-yuesheng.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Du Yuesheng</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Du Yuesheng was a Shanghai gangster who rose to lead the Green Gang and became one of the most powerful men in the city between the world wars.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/dual-kingship"><span class="enc-name">Dual kingship</span><span class="enc-type">Religion / idea</span><span class="enc-snip">Dual kingship is a system in which authority is divided between two rulers.</span></a></li></ul>
